Since your character usually heals much faster, using the stairs
to heal remains a valid strategy for even very powerfull monsters.

The most powerfull monsters know how to cast healing spells on
themselves, I think.  Since no movement takes place while you are
not on a level, they can't cast spells if you use the staircase
strategy.

I use the staircase strategy when first entering the mines.  Any
one monster in the mines is usually easy to take out.  For my
early characters the problem is number of monsters not the hit
points of any one monster.  So I often dip down, kill one and
pick up its corpse and items, go up the stairs, eat the corpse
if I'm not Satiated, wait until I have all of my hit points
again, and dip back down.

